Thumbs.db

# ---- Working notes, kept on the maintainer's machine ----
# The engineering journals and the working notes beside them: French, dated, raw. They are the
# project's memory and a hundred code comments name them, so they are not deleted -- but a public
# repository's history is not the place for them, so they live in one ignored directory and stay
# off the published tree. Anything of that kind belongs there rather than at the root, which is why
# this is a single rule: a working note that appears anywhere else is visible, and that is the
# point. docs/history/README.md says what each file is.
#
# The contents rather than the directory, because git never descends into an excluded directory and
# the two exceptions below could then never match.
docs/history/**

# Two exceptions, and they end with the plan. The release plan and its notes live with the other
# working notes but are still tracked, because the loop that works through them requires an item's
# mark and its note to land in the same commit. Without these two lines `git add` skips them in
# silence, which is how a mark stays uncommitted. They are removed, and the files detached from the
# index, at the plan's closing step.
!docs/history/RELEASE-PLAN.md
!docs/history/RELEASE-PLAN-NOTES.md

# ---- Recorded benchmark runs (bench/compare.sh --record) ----
bench/.runs/
bench/.ab/
